  "cause": {
    "proximate_text": "The direct cause of the code class boundary leakage from the 3/4-inch and 1-inch elbows were cracks in the socket weld, and the apparent cause was high-cycle fatigue. The primary stresses driving the fatigue cracking were likely operating stresses exacerbated by uprates in plant power and implementation of MELLLA+ which resulted in changes in recirculation pump speed. These operating changes increase vibrational loads and can cause pipes and systems to fall into resonant frequencies of the area.",
    "cause_code": "TBD",
    "category": "provisional",
    "theme": "high-cycle fatigue cracking of small-bore piping from vibrational loading (MELLLA+/uprate-driven)",
    "provisional": true
  },
